━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ NameSymbol

` A declared name, and where only some targets' builds see it, the names of those targets.

+ namespace String
+ kind String
+ name String
+ line U32
+ column U32
+ origin-name String
+ origin-path String
+ origin-key String
+ call-shape FunctionCallShape?
+ import-priority = -1
+ import-line U32
+ import-column U32
+ builds [String]?

────────────────────
+ This
    - namespace String
    - kind String
    - name String
    - site SymbolSite

` A name declared at `site`, whose origin key tells its declaration from every other one.
line = site.line
column = site.column
origin-name = site.origin-name
origin-path = site.origin-path
origin-key = "$module-key:$kind:$name:$line:$column"

────────────────────
+ do imported-by NameSymbol
    - priority Int
    - entry ImportEntry
    - builds [String]?

` This symbol as brought in by the direct import `entry`, the `priority`th of its module, in the
` builds of `builds`.
. copy = NameSymbol(namespace, kind, name, SymbolSite(line, column, origin-name, origin-path))
copy.origin-key = origin-key
copy.call-shape = call-shape
copy.import-priority = priority
copy.import-line = entry.begin-line
copy.import-column = entry.begin-column
copy.builds = builds
= copy

────────────────────
+ do shares-build Bool
    - other NameSymbol

` Whether the build for some target sees both this symbol and `other`.
for target in targets()
    if sees(target.name) && other.sees(target.name)
        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ sees Bool
    - target String

!builds || builds.find(target) != null

────────────────────
+ get key String

"$namespace:$name"

────────────────────
